WEBVTT

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:07.470
I can't finish reading the magazine pages

00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:14.380
I get the feeling that I must read it

00:00:16.270 --> 00:00:21.130
Game cartridges are stacked in the corner of the room

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:27.830
Is there no meaning if I don't play them?

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:32.930
You're on the other side of the table

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:36.300
I'm talking to you, but...

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:43.230
You don't change your facial expression at all

00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:49.480
Even though I'm this close to you

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:56.740
These feelings don't reach you, don't reach you

00:00:57.170 --> 00:01:03.490
What is truly precious?

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:17.390
Kaiba boy, if you defeat me, I will release Mokuba boy's soul from this card.

00:01:18.040 --> 00:01:19.490
It's my turn!

00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:20.660
Stop!

00:01:22.420 --> 00:01:30.400
That card is your most trusted card with 3000 attack points: Blue-Eyes White Dragon!

00:01:32.060 --> 00:01:32.920
Impossible.

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:37.500
Pegasus knows my hand?

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:43.850
Kaiba Defeated!
Invincible Toon World

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:46.780
His power...

00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:51.020
Pegasus is definitely reading Kaiba's mind.

00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:53.720
There's no way he can do that.

00:01:53.720 --> 00:01:59.130
Come on.  If that's true, there's no way anyone can beat him.

00:01:59.420 --> 00:02:02.630
But that is the Millennium Eye's power.

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:06.240
Pegasus must have a weakness.

00:02:06.820 --> 00:02:08.840
And I know Kaiba can find it.

00:02:12.220 --> 00:02:16.710
Pegasus can really read my mind?

00:02:16.710 --> 00:02:18.080
That's ridiculous!

00:02:23.020 --> 00:02:26.390
None of the cards in my hand can defeat Dark Rabbit.

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:30.390
I place another card in defense position.

00:02:30.680 --> 00:02:32.500
I end my turn.

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:36.230
It's my turn.

00:02:39.370 --> 00:02:43.570
Kaiba boy, do you like comic books?

00:02:45.110 --> 00:02:49.880
It seems you don't like them.  That's unfortunate.

00:02:49.880 --> 00:02:53.280
But I love them!

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:57.780
I've loved Funny Rabbit since I was a child.

00:02:58.080 --> 00:03:03.130
Those crazy characters with their wild antics on TV are wonderful.

00:03:03.130 --> 00:03:06.600
They've always been my best friends.

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:12.470
They're still happily running around in my heart.

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:14.000
Who cares?

00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:18.080
They will never betray me.

00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:19.780
What are you trying to say?

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:23.300
And they will never die.

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:26.920
I will introduce you to their world!

00:03:28.350 --> 00:03:30.020
My card is...

00:03:43.180 --> 00:03:45.180
Toon World!

00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:48.140
Toon World?

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:49.820
What is that?

00:03:49.820 --> 00:03:52.520
A castle appeared like a pop-up book.

00:03:52.520 --> 00:03:54.710
I've never seen that card before.

00:03:55.060 --> 00:03:58.450
Toon World?  What kind of card is that?

00:03:58.750 --> 00:04:02.700
Hey, Pegasus's Dark Rabbit is missing.

00:04:05.960 --> 00:04:08.340
Where did you hide your Dark Rabbit?

00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:13.100
All my cards have become Toon Cards.

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:16.020
They now live inside this book.

00:04:16.020 --> 00:04:19.840
They're hiding somewhere in this world.

00:04:26.740 --> 00:04:29.820
They'll soon show themselves.

00:04:29.820 --> 00:04:32.670
Dark Rabbit attacks!

00:04:32.820 --> 00:04:34.480
Toon Attack!

00:04:36.350 --> 00:04:37.850
What is that?

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:55.000
Oh my.

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:59.240
Dark Rabbit hid inside the picture book again.

00:04:59.420 --> 00:05:08.150
Oh, I forgot to tell you that once Toon World closes, you can't attack the monsters inside it.

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:09.350
What?

00:05:09.350 --> 00:05:11.040
No way!

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:13.220
Kaiba can't do anything!

00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:15.550
It's my turn.

00:05:15.550 --> 00:05:18.090
I set one card and end the turn.

00:05:20.840 --> 00:05:23.300
It's my turn, Kaiba boy.

00:05:23.510 --> 00:05:26.700
Let me show you something more interesting.

00:05:27.200 --> 00:05:31.210
This is the Blue-Eyes White Dragon that I took from you.

00:05:32.210 --> 00:05:35.710
I play this in attack position.

00:05:58.660 --> 00:06:02.170
My Blue-Eyes...

00:06:02.570 --> 00:06:08.180
All monsters on my field become denizens of Toon World.

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:09.950
What do you think?

00:06:09.950 --> 00:06:12.420
Isn't it more lovable than before?

00:06:13.740 --> 00:06:15.240
What's going on?

00:06:15.240 --> 00:06:16.970
Kaiba's Blue-Eyes is...

00:06:16.970 --> 00:06:19.390
That's the power of Toon World.

00:06:21.820 --> 00:06:26.130
Blue-Eyes Toon Dragon, attack Rude Kaiser!

00:06:34.620 --> 00:06:39.180
Oh my!  I sense tremendous anger in your heart.

00:06:42.180 --> 00:06:45.960
Pegasus. it seems you can read my hand.

00:06:46.420 --> 00:06:49.200
In that case, I'll discard my entire hand.

00:06:49.770 --> 00:06:50.850
What?

00:06:51.060 --> 00:06:56.860
I'll draw the top card in my deck, and I don't know what it is.

00:06:57.080 --> 00:07:00.960
Which means you don't know either.

00:07:01.330 --> 00:07:04.700
I'll place that card on the field in attack position!

00:07:04.700 --> 00:07:06.200
Kaiba!

00:07:06.420 --> 00:07:09.210
Kaiba is getting desperate.

00:07:09.210 --> 00:07:13.080
No, I know how Kaiba feels.

00:07:13.080 --> 00:07:14.440
What do you mean?

00:07:14.440 --> 00:07:17.950
He's entrusting everything into the card he's about to draw.

00:07:18.760 --> 00:07:22.400
Kaiba believes in his deck from the bottom of his heart.

00:07:22.920 --> 00:07:26.390
He has to because of his heavy responsibility.

00:07:27.200 --> 00:07:30.460
Jonouchi has grown up.

00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:32.460
Kaiba.

00:07:32.800 --> 00:07:35.930
Here I go!  I bet everything on this card!

00:07:36.380 --> 00:07:38.400
The card I believe in is...

00:07:44.580 --> 00:07:47.160
Blue-Eyes White Dragon!

00:07:47.980 --> 00:07:52.200
He's amazing!  He managed to draw Blue-Eyes!

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:54.960
Kaiba's cards responded to his wishes.

00:07:54.960 --> 00:07:56.560
That Kaiba!

00:07:56.560 --> 00:07:59.860
I hate to say it, but he's a first-rate duelist!

00:08:00.100 --> 00:08:03.760
Pegasus, you said you sensed my anger.

00:08:03.760 --> 00:08:06.960
I'm far beyond angry!

00:08:09.560 --> 00:08:13.800
It's a battle between a real Blue-Eyes and a cartoon Blue-Eyes.

00:08:14.130 --> 00:08:15.940
Be careful, Kaiba.

00:08:15.940 --> 00:08:20.610
There must be things about Toon World that we don't know yet.

00:08:20.920 --> 00:08:23.150
Wonderful.

00:08:23.150 --> 00:08:29.720
Kaiba boy, you're a lucky boy for drawing another Blue-Eyes.

00:08:30.160 --> 00:08:34.760
How dare you turn my proud monster into something pitiful!

00:08:34.760 --> 00:08:36.460
I won't forgive you, Pegasus!

00:08:36.460 --> 00:08:38.490
Oh no!

00:08:38.660 --> 00:08:44.330
Here I go!  Blue-Eyes attacks using Burst Stream!

00:08:45.970 --> 00:08:47.880
They have the same attack points!

00:08:47.880 --> 00:08:48.970
They'll both be destroyed!

00:09:12.510 --> 00:09:13.700
What?

00:09:14.460 --> 00:09:15.860
Did you see that?

00:09:15.860 --> 00:09:18.100
Pegasus's Blue-Eyes dodged it!

00:09:19.660 --> 00:09:24.980
There are 583 episodes of Funny Rabbit.

00:09:25.800 --> 00:09:33.340
In those episodes, his archrival Bulldog Policeman fired over 26,000 bullets at him.

00:09:33.340 --> 00:09:38.180
But not a single one hit Funny Rabbit.

00:09:38.180 --> 00:09:40.360
It's a miracle!

00:09:43.400 --> 00:09:51.200
As long as Toon World is on my field, every card I play becomes a Toon Card.

00:09:51.430 --> 00:09:55.660
Toons are the perfect life form!

00:09:55.660 --> 00:09:58.940
Then there's no way he can defeat those Toons!

00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:00.860
That punk Pegasus!

00:10:00.860 --> 00:10:05.780
Even if he's the creator of the Duel Monsters, that card is unfair!

00:10:06.200 --> 00:10:08.820
Yugi, did you know about it?

00:10:09.120 --> 00:10:12.760
No.  That card isn't available to the public.

00:10:12.760 --> 00:10:16.640
There's only one copy in the world, and it's for Pegasus.

00:10:16.640 --> 00:10:18.730
Only one in the world?

00:10:18.940 --> 00:10:22.700
It's not fair that he created a card that only he can use!

00:10:22.700 --> 00:10:25.430
It's my turn.

00:10:27.580 --> 00:10:36.320
Kaiba boy, by discarding your hand and drawing a new card, you think that I won't know what you have.

00:10:36.320 --> 00:10:38.580
But that was pointless.

00:10:38.730 --> 00:10:44.590
When a player builds his deck, he subconsciously memorizes his cards.

00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:51.860
Which means I know every card hidden in your deck.

00:10:52.510 --> 00:10:55.860
My turn!  I play this card!

00:11:06.530 --> 00:11:08.280
Shine Palace!

00:11:08.680 --> 00:11:11.560
It's Toon World's newest page.

00:11:11.560 --> 00:11:16.260
Light Attribute monsters gain 500 attack points.

00:11:16.260 --> 00:11:19.020
Toon World's newest page?

00:11:19.240 --> 00:11:20.900
That is correct.

00:11:20.900 --> 00:11:25.530
The story of your defeat is written inside Toon World.

00:11:25.530 --> 00:11:30.770
My Blue-Eyes Toon Dragon gains light energy and powers up!

00:11:44.220 --> 00:11:49.400
Pegasus's Toon Dragon has more attack points than Kaiba's Blue-Eyes!

00:11:50.700 --> 00:11:52.020
Kaiba...

00:11:52.550 --> 00:11:55.690
Blue-Eyes Toon Dragon attacks!

00:11:55.690 --> 00:11:57.960
Burst Stream!

00:11:59.030 --> 00:12:00.800
I activate my spell card!

00:12:00.800 --> 00:12:02.500
Negate Attack!

00:12:07.400 --> 00:12:10.140
Good!  He stopped Pegasus's attack!

00:12:10.140 --> 00:12:13.810
I know all your spell cards as well.

00:12:13.950 --> 00:12:16.810
Negate Attack can only be used once.

00:12:16.810 --> 00:12:21.320
You can't avoid Toon Dragon's attack next turn.

00:12:21.740 --> 00:12:23.320
My turn.

00:12:25.400 --> 00:12:31.600
If I don't do something, Toon Dragon will destroy my Blue-Eyes, and I won't be able to win.

00:12:31.940 --> 00:12:35.730
Mokuba, our fate rests on this card.

00:12:43.500 --> 00:12:46.540
I drew it!  My card is...

00:12:47.460 --> 00:12:49.000
Shadow Spell!

00:12:55.070 --> 00:13:01.020
The dark chains stop your monster from moving, and it loses 700 attack points.

00:13:03.950 --> 00:13:09.460
Kaiba boy's deck only has one card that can defeat a Toon.

00:13:09.460 --> 00:13:12.840
It's impressive that he drew that card at this time.

00:13:13.400 --> 00:13:17.240
The dark chains can stop any monster, even a Toon!

00:13:17.500 --> 00:13:20.510
Prepare yourself!  Burst Stream!

00:13:28.880 --> 00:13:30.140
He did it!

00:13:30.140 --> 00:13:32.490
He destroyed Pegasus's Toon Dragon!

00:13:32.940 --> 00:13:36.090
Seto Kaiba is impressive.

00:13:36.480 --> 00:13:44.140
Blue-Eyes, I would rather destroy you then let you transform into something as pathetic as a Toon.

00:13:44.140 --> 00:13:46.600
Thank you, Kaiba boy.

00:13:46.600 --> 00:13:51.360
I felt the love you have for Blue-Eyes.

00:13:51.360 --> 00:13:56.220
As the creator of Duel Monsters, that makes me happy.

00:13:56.700 --> 00:13:57.940
But...

00:13:59.040 --> 00:14:04.520
Your connection with Blue-Eyes is the reason why you'll lose.

00:14:04.520 --> 00:14:06.550
My card is...

00:14:06.550 --> 00:14:08.790
Dragon Capture Jar!

00:14:12.700 --> 00:14:17.300
All Dragon-Type Monsters are sealed inside this jar.

00:14:31.580 --> 00:14:37.080
Dragon Capture Jar gains the absorbed dragon's defense points.

00:14:37.600 --> 00:14:38.950
That Pegasus!

00:14:38.950 --> 00:14:43.420
I have to destroy that Jar before he gains control of another Blue-Eyes.

00:14:46.500 --> 00:14:49.560
My turn!  I play a monster in defense position!

00:14:53.700 --> 00:14:55.800
It's my turn.

00:14:56.100 --> 00:14:58.640
I set one card on the field.

00:15:00.340 --> 00:15:03.000
And I play Dragon Piper in defense position.

00:15:04.360 --> 00:15:06.600
With this combo, Pegasus is planning to...

00:15:06.600 --> 00:15:10.220
He plans to resurrect the Blue-Eyes that he captured.

00:15:11.450 --> 00:15:12.960
Exactly.

00:15:13.250 --> 00:15:17.500
It will become a Toon again and finish you.

00:15:17.900 --> 00:15:21.190
It will take that "pathetic" form you mentioned.

00:15:21.190 --> 00:15:25.720
How dare you!  I'll crush you along with Dragon Piper!

00:15:25.720 --> 00:15:28.270
Swordstalker, attack!

00:15:28.480 --> 00:15:30.540
Destroy Dragon Piper!

00:15:33.270 --> 00:15:36.900
I activate the spell card Mimicat.

00:15:36.900 --> 00:15:38.230
What?

00:15:38.230 --> 00:15:42.800
This card copies any card you discarded.

00:15:43.700 --> 00:15:46.640
It copies Crush Card Virus.

00:15:48.120 --> 00:15:51.620
I infect Dragon Piper with the virus.

00:15:51.810 --> 00:15:52.630
What?

00:15:52.880 --> 00:15:56.200
He's using Dragon Piper to spread the virus.

00:15:56.350 --> 00:15:58.630
Don't attack it, Kaiba!

00:16:01.250 --> 00:16:04.770
Swordstalker's attack can no longer be stopped!

00:16:07.740 --> 00:16:15.250
Now Crush Card Virus destroys all your monsters with at least 1500 attack points!

00:16:18.620 --> 00:16:21.620
It also destroys all the cards in my deck.

00:16:22.870 --> 00:16:29.630
Your deck is mostly made up of monsters with at least 1500 attack points.

00:16:29.630 --> 00:16:31.580
I can't believe this.

00:16:31.580 --> 00:16:35.170
I never thought Kaiba's powerful deck had a weak point!

00:16:35.170 --> 00:16:36.680
Kaiba.

00:16:36.680 --> 00:16:40.170
Even if he has life points, if he has no cards left...

00:16:42.680 --> 00:16:45.930
I only have one card left.

00:16:46.220 --> 00:16:47.880
Monster Reborn!

00:16:48.580 --> 00:16:52.340
I use this card to revive Saggi the Dark Clown.

00:16:52.850 --> 00:16:57.140
I admire your desire to battle to the very end.

00:16:57.140 --> 00:17:04.430
But if i destroy that monster on my next turn, you'll have no cards, and I win.

00:17:04.860 --> 00:17:06.450
Mokuba...

00:17:07.660 --> 00:17:09.600
Forgive me.

00:17:09.940 --> 00:17:13.360
I attack with Bickuribox!

00:17:24.460 --> 00:17:28.160
Farewell, Mokuba.  Farewell, Yugi.

00:17:34.280 --> 00:17:36.260
Kaiba!

00:17:38.880 --> 00:17:44.000
Since you have no cards left, you lose.

00:17:45.860 --> 00:17:51.160
Kaiba boy, you know what happens when you lose the game, right?

00:17:51.160 --> 00:17:57.350
The loser loses everything he holds dear, including himself.

00:17:57.700 --> 00:18:01.920
You will share the same fate as Mokuba boy!

00:18:02.270 --> 00:18:03.520
Mokuba!

00:18:03.520 --> 00:18:05.520
Mind Card!

00:18:13.530 --> 00:18:17.260
I sealed your mind inside this card.

00:18:17.260 --> 00:18:23.420
You'll now become my obedient servant and serve me.

00:18:23.880 --> 00:18:25.910
The older and younger brother.

00:18:26.170 --> 00:18:32.420
Even though these two cards are close together, your souls are far apart.

00:18:32.420 --> 00:18:38.120
If you both died, you could've been happy by reuniting in the afterlife.

00:18:44.000 --> 00:18:46.500
Take away that empty shell.

00:18:52.580 --> 00:18:55.580
Kaiba has ended up just like Mokuba.

00:18:55.580 --> 00:18:56.640
No way.

00:18:56.640 --> 00:18:57.880
Kaiba.

00:18:58.110 --> 00:19:03.260
Kaiba risked his life to save Mokuba.

00:19:03.260 --> 00:19:04.100
Yugi.

00:19:04.100 --> 00:19:08.390
He wanted to save someone dear to him, just like me!

00:19:09.180 --> 00:19:11.580
Pegasus!

00:19:12.620 --> 00:19:17.730
You have no right to take what's important from anyone!

00:19:21.080 --> 00:19:23.420
Only Yugi boy remains.

00:19:31.960 --> 00:19:35.250
The other Yugi has appeared.

00:19:35.250 --> 00:19:39.620
Pegasus, I will defeat you with my own hands!

00:19:39.770 --> 00:19:47.730
Yugi boy, you must win the finals to earn the right to battle me.

00:19:48.080 --> 00:19:51.300
I know.  But you better be prepared!

00:19:51.300 --> 00:19:55.280
My rage will not subside until I defeat you!

00:19:57.470 --> 00:20:02.810
The championship tournament will take place tomorrow morning in this Duel Ring!

00:20:03.240 --> 00:20:10.720
Out of you four, the winning duelist will earn the great privilege of dueling me!

00:20:11.800 --> 00:20:20.390
Yugi boy, even if you possess the Millennium Puzzle, it's powerless against my Millennium Eye.

00:20:22.160 --> 00:20:24.680
I'll prove that to you.

00:20:30.800 --> 00:20:35.330
Everyone has their own goals as they wait for tomorrow's finals.

00:20:35.330 --> 00:20:39.060
But there's something suspicious about Pegasus's Mind Scan.

00:20:39.060 --> 00:20:41.430
Isn't that a peephole?

00:20:41.430 --> 00:20:45.230
He must've been spying on his opponent's hand from the top of the tower!

00:20:45.230 --> 00:20:50.560
Honda and Bakura, we're going to investigate that tower to help Yugi and Jonouchi!

00:20:50.560 --> 00:20:54.060
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Night Before the Battle!
Pegasus's Secret

00:20:54.060 --> 00:20:55.760
Duel, standby!

00:21:00.050 --> 00:21:08.460
The flask glistens

00:21:09.490 --> 00:21:16.300
Wait for me in the science classroom

00:21:16.800 --> 00:21:25.270
If we put our cold hands together

00:21:25.970 --> 00:21:33.050
And rub them together, they become warm

00:21:34.750 --> 00:21:38.890
Shower of happiness

00:21:39.180 --> 00:21:42.990
I will shower you with it

00:21:43.320 --> 00:21:51.270
I will support you even when you feel lonely

00:21:51.470 --> 00:21:55.500
Shower of happiness

00:21:55.770 --> 00:21:59.640
You are not alone

00:22:00.010 --> 00:22:06.350
You're protected by a giant ring of friendship
